&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps our users extend their online presence to the physical world. The Terminal team’s mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as the Stripe API has made it to accept online payments. Whether a user is building a superb retail experience, extending their website to a pop-up store, or enabling mobile point-of-sale payments at their next event, Terminal gives them the building blocks to do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Almost every Terminal experience starts with a developer building the integration. The Developer Experiences team owns that work: the SDKs, APIs, integration primitives, documentation, and example apps that developers—and, increasingly, AI agents—use to build on Terminal. In this role, you’ll own how developers and agents integrate in-person payments with Stripe, from making their first test charge to running their integrations at scale in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own the roadmap and execution for Terminal’s developer-facing surface: the client SDKs (JavaScript, iOS, Android, React Native, .NET, and Java), the integration primitives developers depend on, and the documentation and example apps that help them make their first successful charge. You’ll work with engineering to ship capabilities that make Terminal faster to integrate and more reliable to run while supporting newer patterns such as server-driven integration and agent-built integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap and execution for Terminal’s developer experience within the team’s strategy: break the roadmap into milestones, define requirements, prioritize work, and drive delivery through sprint planning while making the tradeoffs required by a broad surface area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Talk regularly with external developers, platforms, and internal Stripe teams to validate ideas, requirements, and prototypes and turn what you learn into better developer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and design to ship functionality that delights developers building on Terminal, balancing impact against engineering cost and delivering measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integration primitives developers depend on—including connection tokens, integration authentication, device attestation, and connectivity—to ensure that developers can build secure, reliable in-person payment experiences consistently across every SDK and platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the direction for integrations at scale, from server-driven integration and reusable example apps to agentic tooling that allows AI agents to build and test safely, and maintain a high bar for Terminal’s documentation and accessibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to form a point of view, set success metrics, and determine whether changes are working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate decisions and status to stakeholders and use your technical judgment to help the team make tradeoff decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience or equivalent experience, with a track record of shipping products that solve real user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical expertise gained by building and owning developer-facing products such as APIs, SDKs, or developer tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of driving execution across cross-functional teams within an established product vision and strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to make complex concepts accessible and structure ambiguous problems from first principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across many functions, stakeholders, and subject-matter experts and engaging in healthy, respectful debate in pursuit of shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile SDKs, including iOS or Android, or cross-platform frameworks such as React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, in-person commerce, or hardware-adjacent products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building for AI agents or developing agentic tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and launching zero-to-one products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on approach: you test-drive integrations yourself and improve the documentation before shipping functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Seller Experience &amp;amp; Insights team is responsible for ensuring Stripe’s Go-to-Market teams have the tools, systems, processes and policies they need to sell effectively. We identify friction in how sellers get work done, translate seller needs into scalable solutions and partner across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Sales Operations and Enablement to improve productivity and the quality of Stripe’s customer engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is evolving how Sales Development Representatives identify, engage and qualify prospective users. Agentic workflows can remove repetitive work and help SDRs focus their time on judgement-rich customer conversations. Realising that value requires more than introducing new tools: it requires a coherent end-to-end experience across targeting, outreach, task execution, lead handoff, follow-up, qualification and reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the business experience and improvement roadmap for Stripe’s SDR workflows. You will work closely with SDRs and their leaders to understand how work happens today, identify the highest-value sources of friction and shape tools, processes and policies that make the organisation more effective. Your initial coverage will be &lt;strong&gt;Stripe’s agentic outreach solution and Gong Engage&lt;/strong&gt;, including how these capabilities interact with Salesforce, Orum, Gmail, LinkedIn and supporting routing and data services. Over time, the remit may expand to other parts of the SDR tooling and workflow ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as the connective tissue between frontline sellers and the teams that build and operate these capabilities. You will turn ambiguous problems into clear requirements, prioritised roadmaps, measurable launches and continuously improving workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end SDR experience roadmap across account and contact sourcing, targeting, outreach, task execution, handraiser management, meeting disposition and qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the business product and operational strategy for Stripe’s agentic outreach solution and Gong Engage within Sales Development, ensuring agentic and seller-led workflows solve meaningful seller problems and fit coherently into the broader SDR operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the experience across the hand-offs between Stripe’s agentic outreach solution and Gong Engage, including cadence creation, SDR task execution, prospect responses, meeting hand-offs and downstream activity capture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map current workflows and redesign them to reduce manual work, duplicate actions, context switching and avoidable failure points across SDR tools and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable mechanisms to capture, synthesise and prioritise SDR and manager feedback, combining qualitative insight with product usage, workflow, support and pipeline data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate frontline needs into clear business requirements, user journeys, success criteria and prioritised recommendations for Product, Engineering, Data Science, Sales Systems and Operations partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor the metrics that matter across productivity, adoption, workflow health, data quality, follow-up speed, pipeline quality and prospect experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Development leadership, Sales Operations and policy owners to ensure tooling and workflow design reflects routing, territory, rules-of-engagement and qualification requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build launch and change-management plans with Enablement and Communications so that new capabilities are understood, adopted and embedded in daily SDR work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create governance and operating rhythms for agentic workflows, including release readiness, feedback triage, incident escalation, experiment review and post-launch iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify or consolidate the SDR tooling landscape and develop evidence-based business cases for investment, deprecation or process change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the SDR experience in cross-functional planning and communicate trade-offs, progress, risks and results clearly to frontline teams and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of experience in program management, product operations, revenue operations, sales operations, product management or process improvement in a technology or high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience building, improving or supporting Sales Development or broader GTM workflows, data and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading complex, global and cross-functional initiatives from problem definition through launch, adoption and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how modern prospecting and sales-development workflows operate, including targeting, contact sourcing, outreach, lead routing, qualification and CRM activity capture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to map complex user journeys, identify root causes and translate ambiguous seller problems into clear requirements and prioritised solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, including the ability to define success metrics, interpret workflow and funnel data and use evidence to make trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering effectively with technical teams and communicating across frontline, operational, product and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, low-ego and hands-on working style, with comfort moving between strategy and detailed execution in a rapidly changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change-management skills and a track record of driving adoption, not just delivering a launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in Sales Development, SDR Operations or the design of SDR productivity programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Salesforce and sales-engagement, conversation-intelligence, dialing, enrichment or routing platforms such as Gong, Orum, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator or comparable tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating AI-assisted or agentic workflows, including human-in-the-loop controls, quality measurement and responsible-use guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with experimentation, funnel analysis, SQL or business-intelligence tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of data quality, routing, rules of engagement and the downstream effects of workflow changes on reporting and seller incentives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing enablement, documentation or operating mechanisms for global sales teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for understanding seller behaviour and improving both employee and prospective-user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk team builds trust, an essential ingredient for Stripe’s mission to increase the GDP of the internet. We make it possible for millions of businesses to access and use Stripe’s financial infrastructure while protecting our users, financial partners, and the broader ecosystem from harm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk sits at the center of our users’ and Stripe’s ability to grow safely. We help legitimate businesses access Stripe’s financial services, provide credit to creditworthy businesses, and increasingly help users manage their own risk. We also prevent fraud and financial crime, manage Stripe’s credit exposure, meet our obligations to regulators and financial partners, and enable Stripe’s product teams to launch and grow products safely. To do this, we set the policies and standards that guide how Stripe manages risk and develop the advanced AI, infrastructure, and product experiences that put them into practice for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe’s scale—$1.9 trillion in annual payment volume, equivalent to 1.6% of global GDP, processed across millions of businesses—we face risk problems no other company has encountered. The opportunities and complexities are only growing as AI reshapes what is possible, Stripe expands its product suite, regulators raise their expectations, and we support more businesses in more countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager on the Risk team, you will lead cross-Risk and cross-Stripe initiatives that fundamentally change how Stripe and our users manage risk. You will identify the most important opportunities that cut across Risk’s infrastructure and products, define solutions to our most ambiguous problems, and drive execution from early technical shaping through delivery and adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate as a product counterpart to Risk’s senior technical leaders. You will shape infrastructure and product direction across Risk, connect work that would otherwise remain fragmented, and help product teams across Stripe build on Risk’s capabilities. You will remain deeply engaged in the work, helping teams navigate difficult technical and product decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-leverage problems that cut across teams, turn ambiguity into clear product and technical direction, and establish measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead major cross-Risk and cross-Stripe initiatives from initial shaping through delivery, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead changes in Risk’s approach to using data and AI to accurately identify and mitigate risk at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with engineering, data science, and machine learning leaders to shape architecture, data foundations, models, APIs, and product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help product teams across Stripe build on Risk’s capabilities quickly and effectively while guiding Risk teams toward coherent, reusable infrastructure and product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build alignment among teams with different goals and constraints, resolve difficult tradeoffs, and drive progress without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an exceptional product leader who combines strong technical judgment with product insight, strategic range, and executional rigor. You identify important problems before they become obvious, bring clarity to deeply ambiguous spaces, and mobilize teams around solutions that work across products, organizations, and time horizons. You are deeply curious and stay at the forefront of advances in AI and technology, finding practical ways to apply them to our most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You move fluently from defining multi-year strategy to driving the details of execution. You build alignment and lead transformational work across teams without direct management authority. You earn trust through the clarity of your thinking, your focus on users, and your hands-on engagement in the work. You raise the ambition and effectiveness of the teams and product managers around you without needing to manage them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of identifying and delivering high-impact, transformational product or technical initiatives that span multiple teams and organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to bring clarity to deeply ambiguous problems, set a compelling direction, and drive work through execution and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment across data, machine learning, AI, APIs, platforms, and system architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering deeply with senior engineering, data science, and product leaders to shape both technical direction and product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment across foundational infrastructure and user-facing experiences, with a focus on building capabilities that solve real user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep quantitative fluency and the ability to use data and causal reasoning to understand problems, evaluate tradeoffs, and measure outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence senior leaders, build alignment across organizational boundaries, and drive execution without direct management authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to articulate compelling strategies, influence technical and executive audiences, and make complex topics clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency, intellectual honesty, curiosity, and a low-ego, hands-on working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineering background, preferably with a focus on machine learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying AI and machine learning to complex, high-stakes problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fraud, credit, payments, financial services, trust and safety, or another domain involving complex decisions and asymmetric consequences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with globally distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;From Fivetran’s founding until now, our mission has remained the same: to make access to data as simple and reliable as electricity. With Fivetran, customer data arrives in their warehouses, canonical and ready to query, with no engineering or maintenance required. We’re proud that more organizations continue to leverage our technology every day to become truly data-driven.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is changing how data practitioners write, debug, and ship dbt code. As &lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; for &lt;strong&gt;Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt;, you will set the strategy for how that change plays out in dbt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the vision, roadmap, and outcomes for the end-to-end developer workflow: the &lt;strong&gt;Studio IDE&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Developer Agent&lt;/strong&gt; (our AI coding assistant inside dbt Wizard), the &lt;strong&gt;Cloud CLI&lt;/strong&gt;, and the &lt;strong&gt;dbt VS Code Extension&lt;/strong&gt;. These surfaces are the daily home of tens of thousands of data practitioners, from seasoned analytics engineers to newer practitioners who rely on AI to move faster with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a Staff-level role with broad scope and direct influence on company direction. You will be the key partner to the &lt;strong&gt;Fusion team&lt;/strong&gt;, the engine behind dbt’s next-generation compilation and intelligence. You will decide how Fusion’s capabilities become differentiated developer experiences, and you will make sure developer needs shape the Fusion roadmap. The feedback loop between Developer Experience and Fusion is central to how dbt Cloud evolves, and you will be its architect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who is both strategic and hands-on: a leader who can define where AI-native developer tooling is going, and who is deeply passionate about &lt;strong&gt;AI agents&lt;/strong&gt; and what it takes to build them well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;In This Role, You Will&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set strategy and own the roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the multi-year vision and roadmap for developer experience across Studio IDE, Developer Agent, Cloud CLI, and the VS Code Extension, and translate it into clear priorities, sequencing, and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align developer experience investments with company strategy, product-led growth goals, and the Fusion platform direction. Set success metrics and hold yourself accountable for the outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make high-stakes bets on where to invest, what to build, and what not to build, using market insight, customer evidence, and technical judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead AI agent product development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what a best-in-class AI coding agent looks like for the full range of dbt users. This includes agentic workflows, multi-step task execution, context management, natural language interaction, and guided experiences that meet users where they are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape principles for trust, transparency, control, and evaluation in agentic experiences, so users can rely on the agent for real work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track the fast-moving AI development landscape (Copilot, Cursor, Devin, and beyond) and turn it into a differentiated point of view, not just feature parity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive cross-functional execution and influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Fusion team to co-define the boundary between platform and product, agree on API contracts, and keep roadmaps coordinated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering, design, and GTM teams through a predictable shipping cadence, and keep teams aligned on what matters and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence senior leadership and stakeholders across the company with crisp strategy docs, compelling demos, and clear framing of complex tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other PMs and raise the bar for product craft, rigor, and technical depth across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to users and the market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tight feedback loops with the dbt community and enterprise customers, with particular attention to power users and technical practitioners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use user research and competitive analysis to ground strategy in evidence and bring a sharp external perspective into planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, widely understood developer experience strategy that engineering, design, and leadership are aligned behind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer Agent is recognized as a differentiated, well-regarded AI coding product for data practitioners, not just a feature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer satisfaction and engagement (activation, session depth, feature adoption)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Fusion partnership runs on shared roadmap visibility, clear contracts, and coordinated launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Cloud CLI is a first-class product that developers actively choose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You’re a Good Fit If You Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years of product management experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including a track record of owning strategy and roadmap for developer platforms at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct experience owning developer environment products&lt;/strong&gt;, with an informed point of view on what makes development tools excellent and where modern IDEs fall short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience with AI agents.&lt;/strong&gt; You have built, shipped, or led agentic features (multi-step LLM workflows, tool use, context management, evaluation), and you are passionate about the space. You use AI coding assistants daily and have strong, well-reasoned opinions about what works and what doesn’t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of leading complex, cross-functional initiatives and influencing without authority, including across platform and product team boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong technical foundation: you can reason about system architecture, engage deeply with engineers, and contribute to technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning user research and developer feedback into prioritized, well-scoped product work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, from crisp specs to executive-level narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working asynchronously on a distributed, remote team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You’ll Have an Edge If You Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or shipping AI agent products at the frontier, such as agentic UX, evaluation frameworks, or agent orchestration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with dbt or similar SQL-first transformation frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LSP, tree-sitter, or other IDE infrastructure primitives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CLI tooling and developer workflow automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in open source or strong engagement with developer communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of modern data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery, Databricks, Redshift) and the analytics engineering ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation range displayed on this job posting reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire compensation for the target position and level, and may include sales incentives or target bonuses depending on the role. &amp;nbsp;Our compensation ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Our job titles may span more than one career level. Within the range, individual compensation is determined by additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, relevant education or training, business need, market demands. The compensation range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. Your recruiter can share more about the specific compensation range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;New York Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$243,936&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$304,920 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Perks and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% employer-paid medical insurance&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Generous paid time away from work, including paid vacation or flexible/unlimited vacation depending on role and country, plus paid sick time, inclusive parental leave, paid holidays, including a year-end Global Week of Rest, and volunteer days off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSU stock grants*&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development and training opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company virtual happy hours, free food, and fun team-building activities&lt;/li&gt;
